<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">15 April in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">6 events that happened on 15 April, from 1450 to 1989.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1450 <span class="tih-ago">576 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">French victory at Formigny seals the loss of English Normandy</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">French cannon and cavalry destroyed an English relief army at Formigny. Normandy fell within months; the Hundred Years' War itself ended after Castillon in 1453.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1755 <span class="tih-ago">271 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Samuel Johnson publishes his Dictionary</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Samuel Johnson's Dictionary of the English Language appeared after nine years' work, defining some 42,000 words with literary quotations. It remained the leading English dictionary for over a century.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1817 <span class="tih-ago">209 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">First American school for the deaf opens in Hartford</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Thomas Hopkins Gallaudet and the French deaf teacher Laurent Clerc opened what is now the American School for the Deaf in Connecticut. Its signing community helped give rise to American Sign Language.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1865 <span class="tih-ago">161 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Abraham Lincoln dies of his wound</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Lincoln died at 7.22 am in a boarding house opposite Ford's Theatre. Andrew Johnson was sworn in as president hours later, inheriting the task of Reconstruction.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theatre">Theatre</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1912 <span class="tih-ago">114 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Titanic sinks with the loss of more than 1,500 lives</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The liner went down at 2.20 am with lifeboat places for barely half of the 2,224 aboard. The disaster led to the first International Convention for the Safety of Life at Sea in 1914.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1989 <span class="tih-ago">37 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Fatal crush at Hillsborough stadium in Sheffield</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A crush on the terraces at an FA Cup semi-final killed 97 Liverpool supporters. Fresh inquests in 2016 found they were unlawfully killed and that fans bore no blame.</p></div></li></ol>
